title: The four Ds
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

[[Cambium Carbon]]'s wording for where its wood comes from. On their old Carbon Smart Wood page: "We target wood impacted by the four Ds: disease, decay, disaster, and development."

* ''Disease.'' The tree is sick and has to come down.
* ''Decay.'' The tree is rotting or dying, and is no longer safe standing.
* ''Disaster.'' A storm, flood, or fire brought it down.
* ''Development.'' The tree is in the way of a building, a road, or a lot.

Each is a tree that gets removed whether anyone wants the wood or not. Cambium's pitch is that this wood would otherwise enter landfills, so they work with local arborists and millers to rescue it.

The four glosses above are my reading of the words. Cambium's page doesn't define them.

//Source: Cambium Carbon, "What is Carbon Smart Wood?", retrieved June 23, 2025 (no longer at that address since their rebrand).//

Open question: is a tree cut for development really waste, or was it a choice? (my take)

